    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on May 30, our offensive core is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21), both of whom project as high-ceiling anchors against favorable matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a park factor boost and a prime #2 slot, mitigating the slight talent tax imposed by Yesavage. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a high-output day; his 81.21 score is bolstered by elite underlying xwOBA metrics (0.378) and a generous matchup against Brandon Young. While we remain sensitive to the SB scarcity that defines our strategy, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.03) serves as our most efficient stabilizer, capturing a significant dynamic platoon advantage against Michael King that elevates his floor well above the rest of our mid-tier hitters.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's slate involved the final spot in the lineup, where **Miguel Andujar** (57.21) narrowly edged out **Coby Mayo** (46.00). While **Coby Mayo** benefited from positive park factors, his projected #8 spot created a drag that suppressed his utility compared to **Miguel Andujar**, whose platoon advantage against Griffin allowed him to maximize his efficiency. We are closely monitoring the lineup status for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Kyle Tucker**, **Dominic Smith**, and **Andy Pages**; should those \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions shift downward in the batting order, their efficiency scores will require immediate re-evaluation. Notably, **Kyle Tucker** faces a significant hurdle today in Jes\u00fas Luzardo (3.28 xERA), which suppresses his score to 52.47 despite his typical elite status. With **Jorge Polanco** currently on the IL and **Brayan Rocchio** failing to clear our 40-point efficiency floor, we are betting on the stability of our starting nine to navigate these pitching matchups without forcing low-value substitutions.",
